# nr-office-pdf-render-pages: reduced by the wire audit (t19). Already applied: the module lines and re-exports (contact_sheets, render), the mixdog-office-pdf dependencies (fonts, office-base, rt, tracing) and their lock entries.

## Font bridge for the page rasteriser (in-crate, mixdog-pdf / mixdog-office-pdf; check with a rendered page on a real screen)
render.rs calls render_page with RenderOptions { fonts: None, drawing: None } (mixdog-office-pdf/src/render.rs line 445) because nothing implements mixdog_pdf::oplist::FontProvider and mixdog_pdf::render::FontDrawing outside tests. Until they exist the glyphs of a rendered page are not drawn (only the repainted page numbers of the bottom band). When the bridge exists, paint_page in render.rs passes its FontProvider and FontDrawing in the two RenderOptions fields. A canvas with no registered font draws no page numbers or sheet labels (reported once); the registry passed should be the process's scanned system fonts.

